    {
      "title": "Probability of at Least One 6 in 4 Rolls of a Die",
      "url": "https://www.mathsisfun.com/data/probability-dice.html",
      "snippet": "For a fair six-sided die, the probability of rolling at least one 6 in 4 independent rolls is 1 - (5/6)^4 = 671/1296, which is about 0.5177. The complement approach is commonly used because the chance of no 6 in a single roll is 5/6.",
      "domain": "mathsisfun.com",
      "rank": 1
    },
    {
      "title": "The Complement Rule in Probability",
      "url": "https://www.khanacademy.org/math/statistics-probability/probability-library/complement-rule-probability",
      "snippet": "Khan Academy explains that the probability of an event occurring at least once can be found by subtracting the probability of it never happening from 1. In the classic die example, 1 - (5/6)^4 gives 0.5177469136, or about 51.8%.",
      "domain": "khanacademy.org",
      "rank": 2
    },
    {
      "title": "At Least One Six in Four Dice Rolls",
      "url": "https://www.calculatorsoup.com/calculators/games/dice-probability.php",
      "snippet": "Using the complement method, the probability of at least one 6 in 4 rolls is 1 - (5/6)^4 = 671/1296. CalculatorSoup shows the decimal result as 0.5177, assuming a fair die and independent rolls.",
      "domain": "calculatorsoup.com",
      "rank": 3
    },
    {
      "title": "Expected Value and Probability with Dice",
      "url": "https://www.cuemath.com/data/probability-of-rolling-a-six/",
      "snippet": "Cuemath notes that the probability of rolling a 6 on a single fair die is 1/6, so the probability of not rolling a 6 is 5/6. For four rolls, the chance of at least one 6 is 1 minus (5/6)^4, which equals 0.5177.",
      "domain": "cuemath.com",
      "rank": 4
    },
    {
      "title": "Probability of at Least One Success in Repeated Trials",
      "url": "https://stattrek.com/probability-of-at-least-one-success.aspx",
      "snippet": "Stat Trek illustrates the general formula P(at least one) = 1 - P(none). For 4 rolls of a die with success defined as rolling a 6, the calculation is 1 - (5/6)^4 = 0.5177469136, or 51.77%.",
      "domain": "stattrek.com",
      "rank": 5
    }
  ],
  "query": "1 - (5/6)^4 exact probability at least one 6 in 4 rolls",
  "count": 5
}

