      "url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/1706.03762",
      "snippet": "The 2017 paper by Ashish Vaswani, Noam Shazeer, Niki Parmar, Jakob Uszkoreit, Llion Jones, Aidan N. Gomez, \u0141ukasz Kaiser, and Illia Polosukhin introduced the Transformer and self-attention mechanism. It has become one of the most cited AI papers, with more than 100,000 citations reported across major academic indexes by 2024.",
      "domain": "arxiv.org",
      "rank": 1
    },
    {
      "title": "Google Scholar: Attention Is All You Need - Cited by 100,000+",
      "url": "https://scholar.google.com/scholar?cites=17340508235501931991",
      "snippet": "Cited by results for the 2017 Transformer paper show its rapid rise across machine translation, vision, and language modeling. The citation record lists the original authors Ashish Vaswani, Noam Shazeer, Niki Parmar, Jakob Uszkoreit, Llion Jones, Aidan N. Gomez, \u0141ukasz Kaiser, and Illia Polosukhin.",
      "domain": "scholar.google.com",
      "rank": 2
    },
    {
      "title": "The Illustrated Transformer",
      "url": "https://jalammar.github.io/illustrated-transformer/",
      "snippet": "Jay Alammar\u2019s explainer breaks down the Transformer architecture introduced in 2017 and shows how self-attention replaces recurrence in sequence models. The article illustrates multi-head attention, positional encoding, and the encoder-decoder design that made the paper influential in NLP.",
      "domain": "jalammar.github.io",
      "rank": 3
    },
    {
      "title": "BERT: Pre-training of Deep Bidirectional Transformers for Language Understanding",
      "url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/1810.04805",
      "snippet": "Published in 2018 by Jacob Devlin, Ming-Wei Chang, Kenton Lee, and Kristina Toutanova, BERT built directly on the Transformer architecture from 'Attention Is All You Need.' The paper quickly became influential, driving a wave of transformer-based models that dominated NLP leaderboards in 2019 and 2020.",
      "domain": "arxiv.org",
      "rank": 4
    },
    {
      "title": "A Survey of Transformers in NLP",
      "url": "https://aclanthology.org/2020.acl-main.469/",
      "snippet": "This 2020 survey reviews self-attention, multi-head attention, and the rapid growth of transformer models since Vaswani et al. (2017). It cites key milestones including BERT (2018) and GPT-2 (2019), reflecting how transformers became the dominant architecture in natural language processing.",
      "domain": "aclanthology.org",
      "rank": 5
    }
  ],
  "query": "highly cited transformer attention mechanism paper 2017 2020 attention transformers citation influential self-attention authors year",
  "count": 5
}

