      "snippet": "Authors reported interim vaccine effectiveness estimates for adults aged 65 years and older using test-negative case-control methods across U.S. hospitals during the 2023-2024 influenza season. Overall effectiveness against influenza-associated hospitalization was about 41%, with higher protection against A(H1N1)pdm09 than against A(H3N2).",
      "domain": "pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov",
      "rank": 1
    },
    {
      "title": "Influenza vaccine effectiveness against hospitalization in older adults, 2023-2024 season: multi-site study",
      "url": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/38690421/",
      "snippet": "In this multi-site analysis of hospitalized adults aged 65+ years, seasonal influenza vaccination was associated with a 38% reduction in the risk of laboratory-confirmed influenza hospitalization. The study included more than 12,000 patients enrolled from October 2023 through March 2024.",
      "domain": "pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov",
      "rank": 2
    },
    {
      "title": "Seasonal influenza vaccine effectiveness in adults aged 65 years and older during the 2023-24 influenza season",
      "url": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/38577209/",
