      "snippet": "Python\u2019s `statistics.pstdev()` returns the population standard deviation for a dataset, and `statistics.stdev()` returns the sample standard deviation. The standard deviation is the square root of the variance; for the population version, the denominator is `n` rather than `n-1`.",
